# Configuration

Configuration guides own framework source precedence, typed bindings, profiles, substitutions, and reload transactions. Protocol pages own the settings that are specific to their server wire behavior.

## Choose a task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| load TOML or YAML, apply profiles and environment substitutions, or bind typed values | <GuideRef slug="framework/configuration/sources-and-bindings">Sources and bindings</GuideRef> |
| trigger manual, watched-file, or SIGHUP reload and handle rejection | <GuideRef slug="framework/configuration/reload">Configuration reload</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Use the application identity and directories established by the <GuideRef slug="framework">application model</GuideRef>. Define and validate the initial source set before enabling automatic reload.
